## Divergences

Where two functions use different words for the same thing. **Both become synonyms**; the canonical choice is a logged decision, not the modeller's preference.

| Concept | Function A calls it | Function B calls it | Same thing? | Same grain? | Canonical choice | Approved by |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|

<!-- table:vocabulary-audit.grain-mismatches role=register id=Word -->

## Grain mismatches

**Same word at different grains is two terms.** Naming them apart is often the single most valuable thing the engagement delivers — the client has been having a recurring argument nobody could resolve because both sides were right about different things.

A G1 criterion is the canonical grain **chosen and defended**, with source-system grain mismatches identified as the cause of whatever breaks weekly.

